the revelation that emperor palpatine  had a son  and a granddaughter was one of the  biggest moments in the rise of skywalker  in many ways though it posed more  questions than it answered  chief among which just who was the  emperor's mysterious son  the rise of skywalker doesn't explicitly  reveal how palpatine escaped death  although the movie does drop a couple of  hints when kylo visits hexagol for the  first time  he finds supreme leader snoke clones  floating in tubes  later dominic monaghan's character  beaumont kin  offers a handful of theories of his own  suggesting  dark science cloning secrets only the  sift knew  as it turns out beaumont nailed it  palpatine's return relies on all three  like the star wars movie novelizations  ray carson's the rise of skywalker  expanded edition fleshes out the story  that unfolded on the big screen  including the details of palpatine's  return long story short  he used clones during the imperial era  palpatine set up a secret cloning lab on  the planet hexagon  as he fell down the second death star's  reactor shaft in return of the jedi  he used the force to project his  consciousness into a new body  on the far-off civ stronghold a skill  that the novel implies he learned from  his former master  darth plagueis unfortunately things  didn't go  exactly as palpatine had planned the  novel explains  the secret place had not completed its  preparations  the transfer was imperfect and the  cloned body wasn't enough  apparently the dark side takes a big  physical toll on this process  and palpatine's new vessel burned out  pretty quickly so as the new republic  took control of the galaxy  and the first order accumulated power in  the unknown regions  palpatine's sith followers worked  tirelessly to craft the emperor a new  healthier and more permanent body most  of those experiments failed  but one didn't at least not exactly  the novel says one genetic strand cast  lived  thrived even a not quite identical clone  his son still even that body wasn't  perfect  while his clone survived the sith  experiments he couldn't actually wield  the force  and that weakness disgusted palpatine so  instead of using the clone as a host the  former emperor found another use for him  he set his son free so he could continue  his bloodline through more natural  methods  in time palpatine's son met a woman and  had a daughter whose powers met  palpatine standards  after that the sith lord began making  plans to capture rey  and take over her body which obviously  didn't quite pan out  the rise of skywalker novel's  explanation for palpatine's son  dodges a lot of the more difficult  questions about palpatine's family tree  and while it means that rey's father  isn't technically palpatine's son  it's not without president in the star  wars universe  back in the prequel era for example  jango fett treated his own young clone  boba like a son  this is pretty much the same thing or it  is for now at least  the star wars movie novelizations occupy  a liminal space in the franchise's  continuity  and it's entirely possible that future  projects will retcon carson's work  while disney claims that all star wars  material created  after 2014 are a part of the canon  that's not strictly true  and movie novelizations only seem to  count so  long as they're not contradicted by  other higher profile material  for example there's a scene in alan dean  foster's novelization of the force  awakens in which rey and poe meet for  the first time  but that's no longer canon as it's been  superseded by a similar moment at the  end of the last jedi  as such it's possible that carson's  explanation for rey's ancestry won't  survive in the long term  and this has all happened before too in  the years before disney bore star wars  the emperor had a completely different  son who fell victim to the mouse house's  obliteration of the so-called expanded  universe  i felt a great disturbance in the force  as if millions of voices suddenly cried  out in terror  and was suddenly silenced as told in  paul and hollis david's  jedi prince novels the emperor's  original son was triclops  a three-eyed human with considerable  force powers  however to understand his origins you  actually have to go back to the prequel  timeline  where you'll find a woman named sly  moore a force sensitive native of the  planet umbara  moore was one of palpatine's most  trusted advisors not only was she one of  the few people privy to palpatine's  alter ego  darth sidious and his plan to overthrow  the republic but rumors suggested that  they were lovers too  moore gave birth to triclops after  impregnating herself with  force-sensitive dna  she procured from an anonymous source  which is largely implied to be palpatine  on top of that moore is also responsible  for creating triclops's biggest rival  while conducting her bioengineering  experiments sly created a different  three-eyed mutant named trioculus who  tried to take control of the empire  following palpatine's death  of course there's pretty much no chance  that either j.j abrams or his rise of  skywalker co-writer chris tario  so much as glanced at triclops his story  while writing episode 9.  indeed outside of the david's six jedi  prince novels which are aimed squarely  at children  he doesn't make much of an impact on the  old expanded universe  still there are some striking  similarities between triclops and rey's  unnamed father for one neither of them  got along with their dad  after triklops was born palpatine  banished him to the spice mines in  kessel  fearing his power and his pacifist  philosophy both had children too  while imprisoned triclops fell in love  with a former jedi named kendallina  shortly afterwards kendallina gave birth  to a son named ken  who was later whisked away to a secret  jedi city on yavin 4 by an  unknown benefactor like rey ken who is  the titular jedi prince of the david  saga  was an incredibly powerful force user  and like rey  he was devastated when he learned that  he was palpatine's grandson  finally like rey ken ended up rejecting  his birthright  joining the new republic and training  under luke skywalker  so while both kin and triclops are a  little more than footnotes in star wars  vast  sprawling history their legacy lives on  in the rise of skywalker  at least from a certain point of view  check out one of our newest videos right  here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

